Notebook[{
Cell["Benchmark: KPZ at LO with a flowing f_lambda", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"799448e8-3cf0-469d-b283-3e85be3eefe8"],

Cell["\<\
The Kloss-Canet-Wschebor LO ansatz with three functions of p^2: f_lambda \
multiplies the Galilean-covariant combination dt h - lam/2 (grad h)^2, so it \
sits at i w in Gamma(1,1) and in the cubic vertex, at the momentum of the \
hbar leg. Its flow is the i nu coefficient of d_s Gamma(1,1)(nu, p): d/d(i \
nu) before the frequency integral (design/LOFLAMBDA.md).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5df5acc-8bfc-46e7-8414-e0383f44570b"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
kpzlamDir = ExpandFileName[\"~/sources/FRGscalarMSR/benchmarks/KPZLOLambda\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a6e22122-a8bc-44f7-877f-9c688f521653"],

Cell["1. Ansatz", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a336d19e-052b-4183-958b-8158ad65311a"],

Cell["\<\
\"Functions\" -> {..., flam -> 1}: f_lambda has reference 1. Its f(0) = 1 is \
the Galilean Ward identity (the Protected i w tag), so it has no eta; \
BuildLOEquations checks that its flow vanishes exactly at p = 0.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f5dacdad-55a8-486d-af50-eda38e9a36bb"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamTheory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {h}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim];
kpzlamAnsatz = DefineAnsatz[kpzlamTheory,
  \"Density\" -> fn[flam, hbar] (dt[h] - lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) - nuk hbar \
fn[fnu, lap[h]] - Dk hbar fn[fD, hbar],
  \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}, \"Functions\" -> {fD -> Dk, fnu -> nuk, \
flam -> 1}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8fb6c8ea-9f8e-48b3-88cf-882a7b998519"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamSymmetries = DeclareSymmetries[kpzlamAnsatz,
  Protected[{hbar, h}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"Galilean Ward identity: f_lambda(0) = 1\"],
  Protected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 0, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"h -> h + c (shift symmetry)\"],
  NonRenormalised[lamk, \"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3e0bd3ed-a3b3-4c14-a92e-08ea9c94690a"],

Cell["2. Vertices, propagator, loops, LO equations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"53ed2f03-aa00-4f94-a465-93f100fb422d"],

Cell["\<\
The propagator now has i w f_lambda(q^2): Delta(w) = c0 + c1 (i w) with c1 = \
f_lambda (the causal-pole assumption is f_lambda > 0, on the ExternalMomentum \
card). The f_lambda row has double poles at Q (d/d nu of 1/Delta(w + nu, Q)).\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"483dd331-041a-49ca-bab1-8963b20986b8"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamVertices = BuildVertices[kpzlamAnsatz];
kpzlamRegulator = DefineRegulator[kpzlamAnsatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 \
rn[q^2/k^2], {hbar, hbar} -> -2 Dk rd[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" -> {rn, rd}];
kpzlamPropagator = BuildPropagator[kpzlamVertices, kpzlamRegulator];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"db2054e3-c324-4a33-9f3c-d1553782cb2f"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamLoops = BuildLoopIntegrands[kpzlamVertices, kpzlamPropagator, \
kpzlamRegulator];
kpzlamEquations = BuildLOEquations[kpzlamLoops, kpzlamSymmetries];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8bac6a63-bcb8-4bf9-99db-d40eed3543e6"],

Cell["RunOracle[kpzlamEquations];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5c7cb649-03e1-433c-a04c-e0835caa3870"],

Cell["\<\
kpzlamDims = DeriveDimensions[kpzlamAnsatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> \"nu\", \
Dk -> \"D\"}];
kpzlamAdim = AdimensionalEquations[kpzlamEquations, kpzlamDims];
{kpzlamAdim[\"Functions\"], kpzlamAdim[\"HasEta\"], kpzlamAdim[\"Etas\"], \
kpzlamAdim[\"Linear\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ed84a1bb-203a-47b8-ba80-626cf341c4a0"],

Cell["3. References and checks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a12fcd31-aa7c-4b9e-ad9e-c6493118837b"],

Cell["\<\
f_lambda = 1 against benchmarks/KPZLO; generic f_lambda against the Kloss et \
al. kernels (Reference.wl); the derivative expansion at f_lambda = 1 + x p^2 \
against the Taylor coefficients of the three rows (sign and normalisation of \
the d/d(i nu) row).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"41f68327-103b-46d5-b519-58d23a82cbc5"],

Cell["\<\
Block[{Print}, Get[FileNameJoin[{ParentDirectory[kpzlamDir], \"KPZLO\", \
\"Pipeline.wl\"}]]; Get[FileNameJoin[{kpzlamDir, \"Pipeline.wl\"}]]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{kpzlamDir, #}]] & /@ {\"Reference.wl\", \"Checks.wl\"};
kpzlamResults = kpzlamChecks[];
kpzlamSummary[kpzlamResults]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bbe95de0-8d94-4634-abbe-2cf527bd0096"],

Cell["\<\
If[AllTrue[kpzlamResults, #Pass &], \"all checks pass\", Abort[]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f5fbad67-bca7-4400-8a36-10b10a026957"],

Cell["4. Export (contract v3)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c641ca1d-0132-4a3c-adc3-ea31f49b3077"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython[kpzlamAdim, \"G\" -> alamk^2, \"Model\" -> \"KPZLambda\", \"File\
\" -> FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZLambda_LO.py\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"01aaa9dc-6a3e-4cf8-967b-52181247198a"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"04fbe0e4-f2c3-4959-8406-030f1df259e2"
]
